<title>SWEDEN: AGA says '96 profit falls 31 pct.</title>
<headline>AGA says '96 profit falls 31 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish industrial and medical gas maker AGA AB reported on Monday these 1996 earnings.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			  3,551   vs  2,709</p>
<p> Capital gains			   1,794   vs    601</p>
<p>Profit after fin items,</p>
<p> excluding capital gains	     1,757   vs  2,108</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	   2.70   vs  2.70</p>
<p> Sales				    12,860   vs 13,271</p>
<p>Earnings per share (crowns)</p>
<p> excluding capital gains		5.11   vs   6.31</p>
<p> Other operating earnings		242   vs    231</p>
<p> Operating costs			10,166   vs 10,314</p>
<p> Depreciation			    1,371   vs  1,307</p>
<p> Operating profit			1,565   vs  1,881</p>
<p> Share of income in Gullspangs Kraft   0   vs    243</p>
<p> Interest in other associates	   30   vs     33</p>
<p> Tax					   576   vs    410</p>
<p> Minority interests			  6   vs     14</p>
<p> Net profit				2,840   vs  2,110</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll of 12 analysts showed expectations of 1.81 billion crowns in profit after financial items, excluding capital gains. The company itself has forecast its 1996 profit to be at least 15 percent lower, which means 1.79 billion crowns at the highest.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
